*Note on scope and method:* This is Part 30 of a planned 30-paper corpus, completing the full ten-paper history/anthropology module (HIS-01–10) and the entire planned corpus. This paper''s original research contribution is the EU REACH 2022 tattoo-ink regulation (Section 3, 5, 7, 9, 10), a major, current regulatory development not previously documented anywhere in this corpus, combined with cross-reference to this corpus''s existing OSHA hygiene (TEC-01), laser removal (TEC-10), and dermatological (STY-02) material. Consistent with the corpus plan''s instruction to trace "the material and public-health history of tattooing while separating established evidence from unresolved long-term questions," this paper explicitly distinguishes the well-established fact of regulatory divergence from the less-established claim of resulting comparative health outcomes, and flags the Binghamton compliance-testing finding as significant but not yet independently replicated at scale.
